# The one copairing of the sum `Outcome`: `describe` takes it and matches it once, building a Report by one struct
# expression in either arm; the Report either arm builds is the one it gives back, at its border.

route fits.report.describe
choice describe/?1
step describe/?1/Report()
step describe/?1/Report()#2

line entry > describe call
line Outcome·o > describe value                                   # the match in describe's own body opens it
line describe/?1/Report() > Report@describe/?1 value
line describe/?1/Report()#2 > Report@describe/?1 value
line Outcome·o > describe/?1/Report() value                        # `score`, which the arm's pattern takes out of `o`
line Outcome·o > describe/?1/Report()#2 value                      # `reason`, written in the format string
line Report@describe/?1 > describe value
line describe > Report@describe value                             # the result goes on to the caller

home Outcome·o describe
home Report@describe/?1 describe
home Report@describe describe

side entry left
